<BaseLayout title="Weekly client reporting automation for agencies | AI Workflow Toolkit" description="Build a repeatable reporting workflow with source freshness checks and review before distribution.">
  <div class="wrap"><article class="article page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Reporting · Practical guide</span><h1>Weekly client reporting automation for agencies.</h1><p>Build a repeatable reporting workflow with source freshness checks and review before distribution.</p><div class="article-callout">Principle: document the expected outcome, the failure path and the proof of completion before connecting live systems.</div>
<h2>Fix the reporting contract</h2><p>Define the period, timezone, metrics, data sources and calculations before automating the report.</p>
<h2>Check data quality</h2><p>Verify that each source covers the same period and flag missing or stale data. Do not fill gaps with invented numbers.</p>
<h2>Draft with evidence</h2><p>Include links to source dashboards and distinguish measured facts from commentary or hypotheses.</p>
<h2>Require review</h2><p>Ask the account owner to inspect anomalies, explain meaningful changes and approve the final report before it is sent.</p>
<h2>Verify and archive</h2><p>Confirm delivery, save a dated copy and record the source period. Test missing data, late jobs, repeated schedule triggers and delivery failure.</p>
<h2>Use the toolkit</h2><p>Turn this advice into a structured workflow, then test it with synthetic data before production.</p><p class="article-cta"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/builder/">Build a workflow ↗</a> <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/templates/">Browse agency templates</a></p></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
